WEBVTT

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.690
Let's go and don't cry, funny

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.620
Give me a dumbass dream, please

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.860
Don't touch me, baby

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.060
Freedom, baby

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:38.970
I'm elastic, I want to be chained

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:43.570
Can you feel it? The nonsensical afterimage

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:55.320
Even the moments of points and lines
disappear after failing to show

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:01.060
The sad forefront, an empty sensation

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:06.730
Sweet remnants that tear at my heart

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:12.400
Scattering Polaroids, gathering paranoia

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:17.570
I want you to tell me whose turn is next

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:30.940
If you sleep close to this incomplete
form, you'll understand and see

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.590
Are you all right?

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.290
You need to rest somewhere...

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:49.640
That cellar door...

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.470
I never would've expected
there was a cellar here...

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:05.890
There's water behind those boards.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.630
You know this place?

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:25.910
I grew up here.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.910
I was an orphan immigrant.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:33.720
This church was my home for
as far back as I can remember.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.850
Many other parentless,
immigrant children lived here, too.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.460
Father!

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.800
It's time for breakfast!

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.200
Okay, Joseph.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:04.550
O Lord, please bless this
food we are about to receive.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:09.150
In the name of the Father,
the Son, and the Holy Ghost. Amen.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.810
Amen.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.130
Now, now! You'll choke on it if you rush so!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.630
I don't think we'll need to worry about that!

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:23.290
It's only soup. There's nothing in it.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.100
Oh, so it is.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.640
Here! Have mine!

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.350
Father. We don't have any food left.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:44.320
It's okay, Hanna! Today's the day
he and I go into town to collect alms!

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.350
Right, Father?

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:51.490
Yes. With any luck, we'll be
able to have potatoes tonight.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:55.220
- Oh?!
- Really?! Hurray!

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.640
What's that, Joseph?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.270
It's important to have when going into town!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:08.780
You're so lucky! You always
get to go into town with him!

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.480
Collecting alms is grownup work!

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.020
Okay, let's go, Joseph.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.110
Yes, Father!

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.030
But I gave you money just the other day.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.300
I can't afford to donate every time you visit...

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.200
Please, think of the young children...

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.370
We do participate in various other charities.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.270
We can't donate only to you...

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:41.240
Mother. The poor orphans need our compassion.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.280
Please, give them a donation.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.450
You're such a kind boy, Emile!

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.790
Okay, then! I'll do as you say!

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.420
Offer the nice priest some tea, too.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:05:00.060
Yes, yes. Come right this way, Father.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.100
The immigrant boy can wait outside.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.260
I won't be long.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:19.680
What shall we play today?

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.420
You're letting me choose?

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.390
Guess I'm not.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.320
You filthy outsider!

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.960
Look, he's wearing this!

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.360
That's against the rules.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.850
There!

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.540
You idiot! Not his face! The priest'll notice!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.010
Please be careful on your way back, Father!

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.480
Thank you.

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:57.720
That old bag of bones
shoulda stayed a while longer!

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.380
Let's go!

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.020
Joseph!

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.720
Joseph!

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.490
Joseph!

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.700
Father!

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:20.640
Oh, Joseph! Where did you go?

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.410
Never mind that, Father! Did you
get any alms? Can we buy potatoes?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.180
Oh! They're back!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.850
Joseph! Father!

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.520
Potatoes!

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.680
Welcome back!

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.890
Welcome back!

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.330
What are you doing?

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.870
I'm doing spelling practice.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.370
Why are you doing that?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:57.310
Because Father said that
even if you're a poor immigrant,

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.010
studying can help you rise up in the world.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.420
- Teach me, too!
- Me, too!

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.260
Here! Before you catch cold!

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.390
- What's this?
- This is an "E."

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:18.270
It's thanks to us that you always
get donations, you filthy outsider!

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:20.030
Stay off our streets when you're out...

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.740
Hey, you!

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.600
What are you punks doing?!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.180
Hey, you all right, kid?

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.880
Why are you helping me?! What are you after?!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.260
Sorry, but I'm not after anything.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:50.300
Though, if I had to give a
reason, I'd say it's just my nature.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:54.600
After catfish, there's
nothing I hate more than bullies!

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.480
This is my first time in this town.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.350
Tell me, kid. Where's the
nearest local gathering place?

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.090
I'll show you the way!

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.380
Oh! That'd be great, kid!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:21.960
Outsiders and drifters. Our
town's getting filthier and filthier.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.400
This is the town square!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.640
On Sundays, it's filled
with people selling stuff!

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:33.740
That's a restaurant, and that's
where you can get drinking water.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.740
W-Well, bye!

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.110
Hey! What's your name?

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.250
Joseph.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:44.410
I'm Franz Juchheim. Hold on a minute!

00:08:54.830 --> 00:09:00.460
This is a heartfelt gift from me
to you, for showing me the way.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:07.540
What are these?

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.110
They're called sweets!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.770
Try 'em!

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.900
What are these?!

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:32.530
Huh? Oh, they're called sweets!

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:38.270
How did you get these?

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:41.940
A food stall man gave them
to me for showing him the way!

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.410
He's a really nice guy named Franz Juchheim!

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.450
Okay, make room now.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:51.720
- Make sure they're the exact same size!
- Yes, I know.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.460
You get this piece with the cherry, Joseph.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.920
He gave them to you, after all.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.360
Let the littlest one have it.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:05.800
It's sweet! I've never had
anything this sweet before!

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:09.870
It is! Wow! So this is what "sweet" tastes like!

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.460
- Yummy!
- Here you go!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.770
- Go on, eat it.
- No, I'm giving this to God.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.750
There we go!

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:26.150
Do you think it'll make God happy?

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:29.920
I'm sure He'll love it more than anything else!

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:41.030
Father. Can I go into
town? I want to thank Franz.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.470
Give him this.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:52.510
Tell him that it isn't much, but
may he have God's divine protection.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.170
Okay!

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:02.790
There it is!

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.200
Stop it!

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.860
Let go, you!

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.370
Why, you!

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.140
Why, you!

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.560
Stop!

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:41.000
You damn punks!

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.830
Hey! What're you doing?!

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.510
Franz!

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.860
What happened?! What happened to Franz?!

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.830
Hospital. He's still unconscious.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.940
How dare you do that to Franz!

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:23.670
- What are you doing?!
- Stop it!

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:25.440
Let go! He did this to Franz!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.380
You're the one who did it!

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:32.150
Constable! He stole
pastries from him yesterday, too!

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.150
If you ask around, there
were lots of people in town

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.550
who saw him running off
with a bag of pastries yesterday!

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:42.560
He succeeded yesterday, so he
came again today to steal some more!

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:46.260
All this happened when he was
caught in the act and tried to run away!

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.530
I tried to stop him, but...

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:53.470
What... are you talking about?
Franz is seriously hurt, you know!

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:57.440
How can you lie like that?!
You're the ones who attacked the stall!

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.410
What nonsense!

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.810
Emile isn't an immigrant!

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.380
He would never try to
take pastries from a food stall!

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.980
I don't steal!

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:07.780
That's what we believed!

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:11.650
That's why you could always
count on Mother for donations!

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:15.320
I can't believe I've donated money
all this time to raise liars like this!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:16.390
You can say that again!

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:20.930
Listen! If all the young
immigrant orphans are liars like you,

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:23.900
then we can no longer give you donations!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:31.140
Without their donations, the church will be...

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.740
It's okay, Joseph.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:39.980
If you just tell the truth,
my parents will forgive you.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:50.460
Joseph. Immigrants have pride of their own.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:55.490
Place your hand on the Holy Bible,
swear to God, and tell the truth.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.960
Come, now...

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:08.570
Why did you approach the stall?

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:18.620
Answer me, Joseph. Why
did you approach the stall?

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:23.660
To... steal from it.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:26.680
Did you steal pastries
from the stall yesterday, too?

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:30.120
I did.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:35.600
Who pushed the stall into the canal?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.240
I did.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:40.770
Did everything happen just as Emile said?

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.180
Yes.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:46.880
Why did you do it?

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:52.250
Because... I was hungry.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:55.050
Immigrants are all the same!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.120
Joseph!

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.210
Joseph...

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:34.090
I'm sorry, Father. I stole
the sweets from the stall.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:37.060
You would never steal anything.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:44.370
You only tried to protect those
weaker than you. Isn't that right?

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.030
Please forgive me!

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:54.480
If only I had strength,
I could have protected you...

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.140
Father...

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:09.830
Listen, Joseph. It's time I tell
you about your mother and father.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:14.600
I had always planned on telling
you someday when you grew up.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:20.640
It was on a winter day just
like this, some 10 years ago...

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:23.040
Father! Terrible news!

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.990
Oh, my!

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.200
"Joseph..."

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.760
Father...

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:59.980
They had nothing at all, not
even shoes or food, much less a home.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:03.950
Even so, they tried to live to the very end.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:08.760
They'd ceaselessly walked barefoot
through the snow, toward the church.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:12.530
And then, when they realized
there was no possibility of survival,

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:20.430
they left the one and only thing
they did have, your life, in this world.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:30.370
Yes, Joseph. They used the last
of their lives' warmth to let you live.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.080
Joseph.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:38.250
No matter how cruel the world
may be, there's a reason to live.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.910
I'm sure of it.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:47.560
Franz recovered, but was
sent off on a train shortly after.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:54.300
The young orphans eventually
entered into service and left the church.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.670
I remained at the church.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:00.340
And then, when I was 15...

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:04.240
The Jever River overflowed
and caused a massive flood.

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:05.780
This is bad!

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:08.540
It's broken through the third floodgate!

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:23.030
Women, children, and senior citizens

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:26.430
who had simultaneously lost
their homes and their wage-earners

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:29.060
all sought help from the church.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.980
Hanna! Do we have any sheets?!

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:44.280
We're all out of sheets and curtains now!

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.690
I'm hungry...

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.990
Here's some of my water.
Try to grin and bear it.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.830
Damn!

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:03.260
Father!

00:19:12.350 --> 00:19:17.380
He prayed until the very end...

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.550
...for the people in the chapel...

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:31.820
This can't be happening... Father!

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:39.870
This isn't really happening...
Right?! Say something! Father!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.380
Give her back! She's only sleeping!

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:53.650
Give her back! Please!

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.560
Give her back!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:20:00.530
That woman stopped producing
milk because of lack of food...

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:02.230
...so her baby died.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.800
- Calm down!
- Give her back!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:12.100
Please! Give her back! Give her back!

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:24.340
How can God watch this and not do a thing?!

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:34.890
Do our prayers... Do our prayers not reach Him?!

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:00.520
Gather the injured in one place!

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:01.860
Set up a first-aid station!

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.120
Feed the children first!

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:07.260
Don't forget to disinfect the baby bottles!

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:11.600
Check everyone who feels ill before they eat!

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:14.600
I'm sorry we took so long!

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:16.470
Who are you?

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:18.800
I'm Xargin.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:28.340
And that was how Xargin and I met...

00:21:54.270 --> 00:22:05.390
I dreamed of that day we chased shooting stars

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:15.800
What we had kept safe disappeared like sand

00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:19.870
Just another illusion

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:28.970
Asleep, inside memories

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:32.510
Wish for the stars

00:22:32.510 --> 00:22:41.050
Holding countless wishes with both hands

00:22:41.050 --> 00:22:43.620
A wish for the stars

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:51.570
Quietly by your side, as you sleep

00:22:51.570 --> 00:22:57.200
Yes, right next to you

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:03.180
Holding countless wishes

00:23:03.180 --> 00:23:08.940
Yes, right beside you

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:16.860
Look. Atop a cloud he has come.

00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:19.360
The people look up to him.

00:23:19.360 --> 00:23:22.530
Particularly those who knocked him down.

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:26.670
Episode 14: "A Saintly Decision."

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:29.140
He is the alpha and the omega,

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:31.730
the one who holds the key
to death and the netherworld.
